# Vendored: whisper.cpp v1.9.5 (MIT, see LICENSE)

Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp (tag v1.9.5)
Vendored: 2026-10-14 for Arena Edit M7 (local speech-to-text).

Pruned for a minimal CPU-only static build (arena never enables the
removed backends; they were gated behind options that stay OFF):

- ggml/src/: ggml-blas, ggml-cann, ggml-cuda, ggml-et, ggml-hexagon,
  ggml-hip, ggml-metal, ggml-musa, ggml-opencl, ggml-openvino, ggml-rpc,
  ggml-sycl, ggml-virtgpu, ggml-vulkan, ggml-webgpu, ggml-zdnn,
  ggml-zendnn
- top level: examples/, tests/, bindings/, docs/, ci/, models/, tools/,
  python/, .github/, .devops/, dev/

Kept: the `whisper` library (src/ + include/), the `ggml` subproject
(CPU backend only) and `samples/jfk.wav` (used by the arena test suite
as a 30 s public-domain speech fixture — it ships inside whisper.cpp's
own repository).

Build integration: `ARENA_ENABLE_WHISPER` (OFF by default) in the root
CMakeLists.txt adds this directory with tests/examples off and
BUILD_SHARED_LIBS off; the arena_stt target links `whisper` when enabled.
Third-party warning noise is suppressed per target (-w) so the arena
zero-warning policy keeps applying to arena sources.
